# Bundle-mode posts — origin that serves bundle bytes and receives postMessage
# resize envelopes. Should point at the Supabase Functions host so the iframe is
# cross-origin to the SPA. Set per environment. Note: BUNDLE_PREVIEW_SECRET and
# BUNDLE_FRAME_ANCESTORS are Supabase Functions secrets (set via the Supabase
# dashboard) and are NOT exposed to the SPA.
#
# The BundleFrame component auto-detects the host and picks a serving path:
# a `*.supabase.co` value triggers the HTML srcdoc workaround (the default host
# rewrites text/html → text/plain), while a custom-domain value uses a plain
# `<iframe src>` with clean cross-origin CSP. Flip the two lines below to switch.
#
# Dev (Supabase default host — triggers HTML srcdoc workaround):
VITE_BUNDLE_SERVING_ORIGIN=http://localhost:54321
# Production (Supabase custom domain — plain iframe src, clean CSP):
# VITE_BUNDLE_SERVING_ORIGIN=https://bundles.banodoco.com

# Vibe Mode — 4th authoring tab in /submit/post that lets authors chat with a
# Claude-backed coding agent to author bundle posts. Always on. Requires the
# following Supabase Functions secrets (set via `supabase secrets set`):
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<anthropic key for agent-proxy>
#   VIBE_RATE_LIMIT_REQ_PER_MIN=30
#   VIBE_DAILY_TOKEN_BUDGET=500000
